sted the defendant  told chloe  you're gonna take a nap or i'm gonna  beat you because she wanted to make sure  she could grasp chloe  like any other normal five-year-old  didn't want to take a nap  so she ran away from that bed  and what did her mother do she took  those pajama pants  she threw them over her pulled back  and strangled her with those pajama  pants  in chloe's last moments on this earth  she would fight for her life staring at  her  own mother we know that the defendant  intended to do this act she intended to  cause injury to chloe chandler  there is no other intent when you take  pajama pants and use them in the way  that she did  the judge's decision was based in part  on this so-called confession from one of  thomas's police interviews  and she had jumped out of her bed  and i tried to grab her i tried her long  and she slipped out of my arm  i grabbed the pants and went like this  [Music]  um  [Music]  the defense claimed little chloe  accidentally hanged herself and called  their own forensic pathologist  to demonstrate how she could have tried  to free herself  from the pajama pants there are a wide  variety of situations in which this can  basically form a three-quarter inch in  diameter  transverse mark on the neck one of them  is to have it in this particular  situation  this is probably about 5 8 of an inch  which is a little bit less than three  quarters  but even having something like this  which is basically stretched out  and even maybe which may or may not have  been twisted in any ways  could have certainly made some kind of a  market as well  having the presence of seams as well  where these are  items that are a little stiffer and that  they project could  also make certain kinds of marks in the  neck that would be  narrower  so this particular kind of garment is  is capable of making those kinds of  marks on the child's neck  in my opinion terry  unlike me hindsight is 20 20. do you  think the defense regrets  doing a bench trial 